From 3dfd7f8f1d94abfd1f6fd9864fe36c0acf297a9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:01:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): Sodick wire tank and flushing words from the
 machine file

Two optional wire-machine keys, edm.tank (submerged / non-submerged) and
edm.flushing (high / low), set in the Machine window or by the MCP
edit_machine patch (the one undoable machine mount); an unknown word is
refused by name in the .mch file, the project and the patch.

sodick-wire.cps writes them as the 1998 Mark 21 manual's T words -
T84 / T85 flushing, T94 / T89 submersed / non-submersed machining - after
each threading and before the C word, in the manual's Program Example 1
order (T84, T94, C). Unstated, the program is byte-identical to before.
wire-iso.cps notes a stated ask it has no word for.

Fixes #1499

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
